{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. Thompson. I’m Dr. Lee, one of the vascular surgery team. You’ve been admitted today because we found a narrowing in the artery that supplies blood to your transplanted kidney. We’re planning to do a procedure to open it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, doctor. I’ve had this before, right? Last year they put in a stent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. The stent is still there, but it’s developed a narrowing inside — what we call in-stent restenosis. That’s why your blood pressure has been going up lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ah, that makes sense. My nurse at home said my pressures were high. So what are we going to do now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:08:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do a balloon angioplasty. We go through a small puncture in your groin, thread a catheter up to the kidney artery, and use a balloon to reopen the narrowed area."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:10:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be asleep? I remember last time I was groggy afterward."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:12:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be under light sedation — not fully asleep, but relaxed and comfortable. The procedure is minimally invasive and usually goes very smoothly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And is it safe with my transplant and diabetes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:16:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve taken all that into account. You’ve been pre-hydrated to protect your kidney, and we’ve coordinated with transplant nephrology. Your labs look good, and your blood sugar is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been checking it like they told me. What about the medications I’m on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:20:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue all your usual meds — especially your immunosuppressants like tacrolimus and mycophenolate. We’ll also keep your insulin and blood pressure pills."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And after the procedure? Will I feel better right away?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:24:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Many patients notice their blood pressure improves quickly. But the main goal is to protect your kidney function over time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. How long will I be here?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:27:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most people stay one to two days. We’ll watch you closely after the procedure, and if all goes well, you could go home tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2194-05-08 13:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, that sounds manageable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2194-05-08 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Mr. Thompson, we’re about to head down to the endovascular suite. Any last questions before we start?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2194-05-08 15:32:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, doctor. I trust you. Just let me know when it’s done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2194-05-08 15:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Will do. You’ll wake up in the recovery area, and I’ll come talk to you afterward."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2194-05-08 17:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. You’re in the recovery unit. The procedure went perfectly. We opened up the narrowed part of the artery with the balloon. No complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2194-05-08 17:47:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. Is the stent still okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2194-05-08 17:49:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The stent is intact. The narrowing was inside it, so we dilated it with the balloon. We didn’t need to place a new stent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2194-05-08 17:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my kidney? Is it getting good blood flow now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2194-05-08 17:53:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the angiogram showed much better flow after the angioplasty. That should help your kidney function and keep your blood pressure more stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2194-05-08 17:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. My brother had a heart stent — he’s on two blood thinners. Will I need that too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2194-05-08 17:57:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, actually. You’ll be on aspirin and Plavix — that’s clopidogrel — for at least a few months to prevent clots from forming in the stent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2194-05-08 17:59:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can do that. Any side effects I should watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2194-05-08 18:01:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Mainly bleeding — like if you notice bruising, nosebleeds, or blood in your stool. But it’s uncommon. We’ll keep the dose low to minimize risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2194-05-08 18:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What about the groin spot where they went in?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2194-05-08 18:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It should heal quickly. Keep it clean and dry. You can shower tomorrow. Avoid heavy lifting for about a week to let it seal properly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2194-05-08 18:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No lifting — like how much?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2194-05-08 18:08:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nothing over five pounds — so no grocery bags, tools, or grandkids for a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2194-05-08 18:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ha, I’ll tell my wife. What about driving?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2194-05-08 18:12:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hold off until you’re off pain meds. Probably a few days. Just to be safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2194-05-09 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re doing well. Vital signs are stable, and your labs show your kidney function is unchanged — which is good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2194-05-09 09:02:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2194-05-09 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if you’re feeling up to it. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. You’ll need to follow up with vascular surgery in two weeks for an ultrasound."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2194-05-09 09:06:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my transplant doctor too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2194-05-09 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, definitely. Keep all your regular appointments. They’ll monitor your kidney and adjust meds as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2194-05-09 09:10:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, doctor. Thank you — I feel much better knowing we caught this early."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2194-05-09 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. You did great. Just take it easy for a few days, watch the incision, and call us if anything seems off — like swelling, fever, or bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2194-05-09 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2194-05-09 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. Thompson. Get some rest at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2194-05-09 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I plan to — maybe even put my feet up like you said."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2194-05-09 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. That’s exactly what I like to hear."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2194-05-08 12:30:00",
    "admission_end": "2194-05-09 16:26:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 60-year-old male with a history of kidney transplantation, type 2 diabetes, hypertension, and hyperlipidemia was admitted for symptomatic in-stent restenosis of the right transplanted renal artery, presenting with elevated blood pressure. Ultrasound confirmed increased renal artery velocities. The patient underwent elective balloon angioplasty of the stenotic segment via right femoral access, with successful restoration of blood flow and no procedural complications. He remained hemodynamically stable throughout, with preserved renal function post-procedure. Pain was controlled, and he tolerated diet and ambulation well. He was discharged home on dual antiplatelet therapy, antihypertensives, immunosuppressants, and insulin, with instructions for wound care, activity restrictions, and follow-up with vascular surgery and transplant nephrology.",
    "problems": [
      "Other complications due to genitourinary device, implant, and graft",
      "Kidney replaced by transplant",
      "Atherosclerosis of renal artery",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Hyperplasia of prostate, unspecified, without urinary obstruction and other lower urinary symptoms (LUTS)",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of other urinary organs",
      "Surgical operation with implant of artificial internal device causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication,without mention of misadventure at time of operation"
    ]
  }
}
